//! MUST NOT COMPILE.
//!
//! A branch of the wrong depth for its fork (security invariant 6).
//!
//! Capella's state is 5 levels and `block_roots` is 13, so a recent-path proof
//! is exactly 18 siblings. The branch below has 19 -- the length an Electra or
//! Fulu proof would have. A 19-level branch against an 18-level position walks
//! one level past the root, and a verifier that zero-pads or truncates instead
//! of rejecting would accept a proof of a node that is not the one it meant.
//!
//! Nothing in this file says 18. The length comes from
//! `block_root_proof_len<Capella>()`, which is derived from the field count, so
//! the diagnostic prints a number the author never wrote.

use verife::layout::{Capella, RecentProof}

pub fn main() {
    let _ = RecentProof<Capella> { branch: [0; 19] }
}
